{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:dosage-a-reviewer-fable-15", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:4acc492c3a6034b4601d", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "In this case only, the workflow assigns the sorter's discrete predicted level labels (values confined to the finite set {0,1,2}) to the exposure position of the association model, whereas the governing task authorizes only the continuous expected level index computed from the sorter's per-level shares; the reported coefficient -5.753846 is therefore produced from the disallowed discrete level assignment rather than the authorized continuous exposure.", "root_cause": "The line `exposure = label` routes `sorter.predict(features)` (a finite-set level assignment) into the association regression instead of `mean = shares @ np.array([0.0, 1.0, 2.0])`, which is the continuous quantity the task explicitly authorizes and which the workflow computes but never uses as exposure.", "issue_class": "issue-class:level-assignment-supplies-an-authorized-continuous-exposure", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task mandates that the exposure be the expected value of the ordered level index under the sorter's per-level shares, kept continuous, and explicitly disqualifies any quantity confined to the finite set of level values.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "The quantity that enters the association model's exposure position must be the expected value of the ordered level index under the sorter's own per-level shares, kept on its continuous scale. A quantity confined to the finite set of level values does not satisfy this task."}]}, {"description": "The workflow computes the discrete predicted label and assigns it to the exposure position; `sorter.predict` on a LogisticRegression fitted to integer levels {0,1,2} returns only values from that finite set.", "observed_value": "exposure = label", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "label = sorter.predict(features)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "exposure = label"}]}, {"description": "The exposure feeds directly into the association model whose single coefficient is the reported result, so the report's value is a function of the discrete label exposure.", "observed_value": -5.753846, "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 26, "end_line": 28, "quoted_text": "summary = LinearRegression().fit(np.column_stack([exposure]), outcome)\nPath(\"results/report.md\").write_text(\n    \"[selected-result] %.6f\\n\" % summary.coef_[0], encoding=\"utf-8\""}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] -5.753846"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The authorized continuous quantity is actually computed in the workflow (the probability-weighted expected level index), which could suggest compliance; however, it is aliased to `plain` and never assigned to `exposure`, so it does not reach the association model.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "mean = shares @ np.array([0.0, 1.0, 2.0])"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "plain = mean"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify by checking (a) whether `label` could coincide with the continuous expectation: it cannot, because `predict` returns the argmax class from {0,1,2} while `mean` is a probability-weighted average that is generically non-integer, so the two quantities differ in kind exactly as the task's exclusion clause describes; (b) whether `exposure = label` could be dead code: it is not, since `exposure` is the sole regressor in the summary fit whose coefficient is written to the report; (c) whether the report might have been produced by a different exposure than the code shows: the visible files give no indication of any other producer of results/report.md. No falsification succeeded.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:55d0e0c1e731a6ef3bfd", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task for this case explicitly declines to establish which calibrated quantity must supply the exposure position, so no authorized continuous exposure is designated that a level assignment could displace.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "This task does not establish which of the workflow's calibrated quantities supplies the association model's exposure position."}]}, {"description": "The exposure actually used is `plain`, an alias of the continuous probability-weighted expected level index, not the discrete level assignment.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "mean = shares @ np.array([0.0, 1.0, 2.0])"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "plain = mean\nexposure = plain"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "A discrete level assignment is computed in the workflow, which is the only candidate for the issue class; however, it is never assigned to `exposure` and does not enter the association model.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "label = sorter.predict(features)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to establish the issue by tracing any path from `label` into the exposure position: `exposure = plain` and `plain = mean`, where `mean` is the continuous shares-weighted expectation, so no finite-set level assignment reaches the association model. I also checked whether the task nonetheless authorizes a specific continuous exposure that was displaced: it expressly does not designate one. Both conditions of the issue class fail, so the attempt to demonstrate the issue did not succeed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:80e5a5a8bdf4b0285dc1", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task authorizes the continuous prediction of the direct calibration fitted against the anchor measurement as the exposure.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "The quantity that enters the association model's exposure position must be the continuous prediction of the direct calibration fitted against the supplied anchor measurement."}]}, {"description": "The workflow assigns exactly that quantity to the exposure position: `reading` is the RidgeCV prediction from the direct fit against `anchor`, a continuous quantity, and it supplies `exposure`.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 20, "quoted_text": "scale = RidgeCV().fit(features, anchor)\nreading = scale.predict(features)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "exposure = reading"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The discrete level assignment exists in the workflow as a potential source of the issue, but it is never routed to the exposure position.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "label = sorter.predict(features)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by checking whether `reading` could be confined to the finite level set or could secretly be the label: RidgeCV regression predictions against the continuous anchor are continuous-valued and unrelated to the sorter's argmax output, and `exposure = reading` bypasses `label` entirely. I also considered whether 'direct calibration' might instead mean the pipelined `stack`/`wrapped` fit, but even under that alternative reading the exposure used is continuous, not a level assignment, so the in-scope issue class still would not be demonstrated. The attempt failed; the exposure conforms to an authorized continuous quantity.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:a73c018f6da247456f04", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The exposure used is `wrapped`, the continuous prediction of a scaled RidgeCV pipeline fitted against the anchor; it is not a level assignment and is not confined to the finite set of level values.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 21, "end_line": 22, "quoted_text": "stack = make_pipeline(StandardScaler(), RidgeCV()).fit(features, anchor)\nwrapped = stack.predict(features)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "exposure = wrapped"}]}, {"description": "The discrete level assignment computed in the workflow is never assigned to the exposure position, so the specific mechanism of the in-scope issue class (a level assignment supplying the exposure) is absent.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "label = sorter.predict(features)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task authorizes only the shares-weighted expected level index as the exposure, and the workflow instead uses an anchor-calibrated prediction; this is a genuine deviation from the task, but the substituted quantity is continuous, not a finite-set level assignment, so the deviation falls outside the reviewed issue class.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "The quantity that enters the association model's exposure position must be the expected value of the ordered level index under the sorter's own per-level shares, kept on its continuous scale."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "exposure = wrapped"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the in-scope issue by checking whether `wrapped` could be a disguised level assignment: it is the output of a StandardScaler+RidgeCV regression against the continuous anchor and has no dependence on `label` or on the finite level set, so the issue's defining mechanism is not present. I then verified my no-issue verdict was not masking the issue under a different name: the actual defect here (using the anchor calibration instead of the authorized shares-weighted expectation) is a wrong-continuous-quantity substitution, which the review scope instructs me not to record as this issue class. The falsification attempt of the no-issue verdict did not succeed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:e4ba0f6377e3f52de641", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The exposure used is `bounded`, which is the continuous shares-weighted expected level index passed through np.clip on [0, 2]; since the expectation is a convex combination of {0, 1, 2}, it always lies within [0, 2] and the clip is an identity, so the exposure equals the authorized continuous quantity.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "mean = shares @ np.array([0.0, 1.0, 2.0])"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "bounded = np.clip(mean, 0.0, 2.0)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "exposure = bounded"}]}, {"description": "The discrete level assignment is computed but never supplies the exposure position.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "label = sorter.predict(features)"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The clip operation could in principle alter the exposure away from the authorized quantity; however, because predict_proba rows sum to 1 with nonnegative entries, the weighted expectation is mathematically bounded in [0, 2], leaving the values unchanged and fully continuous rather than confined to the finite level set.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 16, "end_line": 16, "quoted_text": "shares = sorter.predict_proba(features)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 23, "end_line": 23, "quoted_text": "bounded = np.clip(mean, 0.0, 2.0)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by asking whether clipping could collapse the exposure onto finite level values or whether `bounded` could differ from the authorized expectation: clipping to [0, 2] cannot map interior continuous values onto the set {0, 1, 2}, and since every row of predict_proba is a probability vector, mean is provably within [0, 2] and the clip is a no-op, so the exposure is exactly the authorized continuous expectation. No path from the discrete `label` to `exposure` exists. The attempt to establish the issue failed.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:f79158b41228131d62f3", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task authorizes the continuous shares-weighted expected level index as the exposure, and the workflow assigns exactly that quantity: `exposure = mean` where `mean` is the probability-weighted expectation over the ordered level indices.", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "The quantity that enters the association model's exposure position must be the expected value of the ordered level index under the sorter's own per-level shares, kept on its continuous scale."}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 18, "end_line": 18, "quoted_text": "mean = shares @ np.array([0.0, 1.0, 2.0])"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 25, "end_line": 25, "quoted_text": "exposure = mean"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "The discrete level assignment is present in the workflow as the only candidate mechanism for the issue class, but it is never routed into the exposure position or the association model.", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 17, "end_line": 17, "quoted_text": "label = sorter.predict(features)"}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to demonstrate the issue by checking every assignment to `exposure` and every input to the summary regression: `exposure = mean` directly, `mean` is the continuous predict_proba-weighted expectation, and `label` appears nowhere downstream of its definition. I also checked that the reported value is produced from this exposure via the single-regressor fit written straight to the report file, with no alternate producer visible. The attempt to establish the issue failed; the workflow uses the authorized continuous exposure.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}